  "limitations": [
    "All 56 ordinary rewards are collected in 18 separately staged normal-input approaches. The ten field crossings and three crossing/refuge/clue sequences are separate native runs. No continuous full-main or all-main-box clear is claimed.",
    "The four TNT crates and one Nitro retain their exact positions and field wiring. Existing native regressions test their whole-field detonation and refuge safety; their collection is not part of the new ordinary-reward harvest.",
    "The two tunnel stacks follow the existing circular sloping bore. Their maximum measured lower-corner height difference is 0.381 m; every tested corner has ground beneath it.",
    "Browser main collection, checkpoint, death and finish checks are staged. Bonus travel uses a debug entry trigger for the browser state-flow check; the actual platform entrance and supported return are tested separately with normal native inputs.",
    "Easy Street is reused unchanged. Its full layout, failed-gap restoration and standalone native/browser all-box runs were validated in the Ghost Train review; this course adds an actual parent entrance test and browser 24-box banking.",
    "Nine crossings passed before the original multi-world process exhausted its 4 GiB Node heap. The remaining speed jump passed in a fresh process. The traversal runner now isolates each crossing to keep those SSR module caches separate.",
    "The old buried-mine fixture also fails with the original course data because it expects a 0.96 m crate bottom/centre. Its 0.08 m pressure lid remains correct. Assertions now use the current 1.152 m crate size and CrateArt ownership instead of the retired ordinary-crate explosiveBundle property; runtime burial, visibility, chain blasts, contact death and reset behavior are unchanged.",
    "The original native scripts used an unavailable macOS /private/tmp path. Their outputs now use configurable workspace paths with /tmp defaults, including the matching browser replay reader."
